+## Explain existing v0.2 evidence (non-normative)
+
+`python3 -m tools.airep_v02 explain --input examples/v02/fixtures/complete.json`
+renders a claim matrix; add `--json` for the same semantics as JSON. It accepts
+the same artifact-array input and operator options as `reconcile`, including
+`--bindings`, `--revocation`, `--independence-policy` and `--profile-bases`.
+`--out` writes either format to a new file. Exit zero means evaluation completed,
+including negative results. Saved reconciliation output is not an input format.
+
+This is a **derived explanatory view, not a new AIREP conformance layer**.
+Claim names, context fields and `explanatory_status` are NON-NORMATIVE rendering
+labels. Native checks, statuses, counts and all per-record class channels remain
+visible. A null native status plus explanatory `NOT_EVALUATED` marks enforcement
+and relying-party claim predicates that the reconciler does not evaluate; no
+acceptance rule is invented. Signature validity is not event truth; MISSING is
+not non-occurrence. See the [worked example](../../examples/v02/EXPLAIN.md) for
+commands, field meanings and the enforcement/effect boundary.
